WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.845 --> 00:00:04.502
In the office the designer draws the filling unit for line 3.

2
00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:07.461
In the workshop the maker makes its plate.

3
00:00:08.535 --> 00:00:11.855
A drawing tells the maker what to make and how exact.

4
00:00:12.602 --> 00:00:16.004
A control loop keeps the level in the tank at its target.

5
00:00:17.044 --> 00:00:19.134
Four topics follow the filling unit.

6
00:00:19.894 --> 00:00:22.332
The first two are about the drawing for the maker.

7
00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:25.983
The last two are about the diagram of the plant

8
00:00:26.076 --> 00:00:28.642
and the control that keeps it at its value.

9
00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:32.672
The first topic is Reading a technical drawing.

10
00:00:33.406 --> 00:00:35.925
The maker was not there and has only the drawing.

11
00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:41.170
The plate is drawn in views, from the front, from above and from the side.

12
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.627
The maker reads the dimensions, because a print may be shrunk.

13
00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:49.678
There we first read the title block at the bottom right,

14
00:00:49.876 --> 00:00:52.175
because it holds the revision of the drawing.

15
00:00:53.507 --> 00:00:56.990
The second topic is Tolerances and G D and T.

16
00:00:57.688 --> 00:01:01.217
The four holes of the plate must fit the four bolts of the frame.

17
00:01:02.255 --> 00:01:06.203
Every dimension may differ a little, and that little is the tolerance.

18
00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:09.870
If a hole is too far off, the bolt will not fit.

19
00:01:10.955 --> 00:01:13.149
There we read the feature control frame.

20
00:01:14.147 --> 00:01:16.597
It says which datums the maker measures from.

21
00:01:17.316 --> 00:01:20.056
So the maker and the customer measure the same way.

22
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:25.837
The third topic is P and I Ds, schematics and the control system.

23
00:01:26.539 --> 00:01:29.140
The tank supplies the product for the filling unit.

24
00:01:30.213 --> 00:01:35.287
A P and I D shows what is connected to what, and how it is measured and controlled.

25
00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:39.335
At the tank that is a level meter and a control valve.

26
00:01:40.384 --> 00:01:43.379
There we read the tag number of every instrument.

27
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.190
The operator walks along the tank with the drawing.

28
00:01:47.913 --> 00:01:50.398
A valve that is not on it is a surprise.

29
00:01:51.707 --> 00:01:54.702
The fourth topic is Control loops and PID.

30
00:01:55.379 --> 00:01:59.988
With every filling the level in the tank drops, but it has to stay at its value.

31
00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:02.386
A sensor measures the level.

32
00:02:03.065 --> 00:02:07.210
The controller compares it with the target and opens or closes the valve.

33
00:02:08.242 --> 00:02:10.761
There we often use a PID controller.

34
00:02:11.762 --> 00:02:13.608
The level stays at its value.

35
00:02:14.338 --> 00:02:19.458
Now the makers can go on, because frame, plate and tank are together on one drawing.

36
00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:22.048
This is the whole map.

37
00:02:22.752 --> 00:02:26.781
Drawings and control is the fourth station of Making things.

38
00:02:27.806 --> 00:02:29.536
Every topic has four levels.

39
00:02:30.532 --> 00:02:33.957
Start with Reading a technical drawing, at Basics level.

40
00:02:34.706 --> 00:02:37.365
That lesson shows where to begin on a drawing.

41
00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:42.903
At Working knowledge level it is about assembly drawings, G D and T,

42
00:02:43.112 --> 00:02:45.411
the PLC and the feel for control.

43
00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.404
At Advanced level it is about threads and roughness,

44
00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:53.444
form tolerances, electrical diagrams and tuning a loop.

45
00:02:54.471 --> 00:02:57.234
At Expert level it is about drawing control,

46
00:02:57.362 --> 00:03:01.240
drawing disputes, protection functions and loop performance.

47
00:03:02.245 --> 00:03:05.995
Every lesson and film in this module has a place on this map.
